//! A small board in a case for the case model's fit check (ADR 0109) and the editor's recipes.
//! Its physical file, `case_fit.physical.nsm`, names the case's two STEP files in `case_fit/`
//! (a box with a boss under one mounting hole, and a lid), written by hand for these tests.
//! The layout file beside it puts a header too tall for the lid (`case_collision`), one of
//! unknown height under the lid (`case_unchecked`), one at the right edge, near the wall and
//! behind it (`case_clearance`, `case_reach`), and two mounting holes, one with no boss
//! (`case_boss`).

import std::parts::connector::{Header1x2, Header2x3}
import std::mfg::jlcpcb::TwoLayer

board Cased {
    .process: TwoLayer {
        .stackup.thickness &= 1.6mm
    }
    .tall: Header1x2
    .edge: Header1x2
    // A 2x3 header has no catalog row, so it has no height from one (ADR 0094).
    .bare: Header2x3
}
